5p + j &= 182 \\
\end{align*}

Notice that the equations above are written in slope-intercept form (that is, in the form $y = mx + b$). The $y$-intercepts of these two lines are 124 cents and 182 cents, respectively. Since the slope of both lines is 0, it follows that the lines are parallel. Therefore, any point on one of the lines must also lie on the other line. This means that the value of $p$ is equal to the difference in the y-intercepts (in cents). That is, $p = 182 - 124 = \boxed{58}$.

