j &= 124 - 3p \\
j &= 182 - 5p \\
\end{align*}Since $j$ appears on both sides of both equations, we can simply plug in 182 for $j$ in the first equation above and solve for $p$, and then plug in $p$ into the second equation and solve for $j$. It follows that $p = 58$.
